<title>USA: NYCE cotton called to open flat to 0.20 lower.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton called to open flat to 0.20 lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures were called to open unchanged to 0.20 cent a lb weaker Wednesday, based on market orders at 1016 EST, floor sources said.</p>
<p>They blamed anticipated losses on the market's failure to maintain gains Tuesday, when March ended down 0.15 at 75.11, traded 75.50 to 74.90.</p>
<p>The back months settled 0.08 lower to 0.45 higher.</p>
<p>Volume was estimated at 10,000 lots.</p>
<p>((--Suzanne Rostler, New York Commodities, 212 859 1640))</p>
